      ],
      "uz_compare": "O'zbekchada fe'l otdan oldin '-adigan' shaklini oladi: 'yeyiladigan taom', 'yashaydigan do'st'. Koreyschada buning uchun -는 qo'shiladi: 먹는 음식, 사는 친구. Sifatlar esa -(으)ㄴ oladi: 큰, 작은.",
      "compare_en": "English puts a 'that / who' clause after the noun: 'food that people eat', 'a friend who lives in Seoul'. Korean puts the verb with -는 before the noun: 먹는 음식, 사는 친구. Adjectives take -(으)ㄴ instead: 큰, 작은."
